WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:04.340
"The Green Knight" seems just about as far-fetched
as a movie can be.

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:08.760
Fortunately, it's also one of the most interesting
upcoming big-screen offerings out there.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:12.730
Its first trailer has dropped, and it makes
clear that fans are right to expect great

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:13.730
things.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.080
Let's take a moment to break it down.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.140
The teaser opens with the Knights of the Round
Table in Camelot, and their ruler, King Arthur,

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:22.410
requests entertainment for himself and his
queen.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:26.850
In a textbook case of "be careful what you
ask for," a monstrous, green knight who looks

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:31.130
like he's made out of wood steps in and challenges
a knight to take a free shot at him.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:35.770
The young Sir Gawain, played by Dev Patel,
is quick to accept the challenge and decapitates

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:36.770
the strange visitor.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:40.760
It’s at this point that the Green Knight
picks up his head and proclaims:

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:45.629
"One year hence."

00:00:45.629 --> 00:00:49.710
As the rest of the trailer makes clear, this
means Gawain must meet the monster in a year

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:52.489
to complete the game and receive a blow in
turn.

00:00:52.489 --> 00:00:55.780
It's pretty clear that the Green Knight enters
the castle with full knowledge that he was

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.940
setting his opponent up, not least because
he delivers a pitch-perfect evil laugh as

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:02.449
he flees in full Headless Horseman mode.

00:01:02.449 --> 00:01:06.280
While Gawain might be concerned with the fact
that his days are numbered, the trailer makes

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:10.540
sure that the viewer can't help but wonder
exactly what the Green Knight is all about.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:16.340
The year has almost passed, and Gawain seems
intent on setting the whole Green Knight incident

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:17.340
aside.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.200
However, his king doesn't want to hear any
of it.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:23.680
In a meeting between Gawain and Arthur, the
ruler states in fairly clear terms that Gawain

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.940
must find the Green Knight to fulfill his
pact.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:28.330
And, just like that, a quest is given.

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:32.030
Because the Green Knight survived Gawain's
blow, and the mythical King of Britons turns

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:36.090
out to be a completionist, the young knight
has no choice but to leave the confines of

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:40.680
Arthur's stronghold and travel through a land
that's unlike anything he's seen before.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.670
It's a solid, and ominous, start for an epic
adventure.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:49.939
As Sir Gawain rides toward an unfortunate
fate, a creepy voice speaks ill of his chances

00:01:49.939 --> 00:01:50.939
for survival.

00:01:50.939 --> 00:01:55.380
It's easy to assume that the raspy whisper
belongs to a soothsayer or witch of some sort,

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.469
but the source of these pessimistic predictions
turns out to be an otherwise perfectly cute

00:01:59.469 --> 00:02:03.060
and furry fox that, for some reason, chooses
to hang out with Gawain.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.469
It appears that whatever fate awaits the young
knight, the fox isn't particularly happy about

00:02:07.469 --> 00:02:08.469
it.

00:02:08.469 --> 00:02:10.050
“Why do you stop me?”

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:12.760
“Your doom is at hand.”

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:16.562
Since the very next thing we see is Gawain
swinging his ax at the camera, and the shot

00:02:16.562 --> 00:02:20.450
looks a whole lot like it might be from the
fox's point of view, it's unclear if the fox

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:23.390
is trying to warn the knight of a threat,
or making one.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:27.530
Either way, a talking fox seems like a pretty
cool creature in the movie's heavy fantasy

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:30.240
setting, and we can only hope that it won't
meet its doom.

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:35.430
The Green Knight is a pretty star-studded
production, and the trailer features all sorts

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:38.040
of legendary characters and amazing creatures.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:42.319
Even so, one of its most threatening figures
seems to be entirely human, though not any

00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:43.819
less dangerous for it.

00:02:43.819 --> 00:02:47.690
Right after the fox has given its warnings
and Gawain swings his ax, the trailer introduces

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:48.690
the Scavenger.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:53.190
This character is a bandit who manages to
tie Gawain up and steal his massive weapon.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:57.510
The fact that the Scavenger and his men manage
to defeat a knight of the Round Table is one

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.510
thing.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:01.850
The fact that he appears to be aware of Gawain's
quest takes things to a completely different

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:02.850
level.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:08.750
As Sir Gawain climbs a hill, he observes a
misty vista, over which a group of gigantic,

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:12.000
shadowy figures slowly march toward an unknown
destination.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.510
Gawain doesn't seem awfully surprised or shocked
to see them, and in the very next moment,

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:19.470
he lifts his ax and appears to scream triumphantly.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:23.019
It creates the impression that Gawain has
been actively seeking out these giants or

00:03:23.019 --> 00:03:27.310
at least knows what they are and is very pleased
to witness their travels in person.

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:31.569
Eagle-eyed viewers will also note that the
fox from earlier seems to be by his side.

00:03:31.569 --> 00:03:35.799
As such, there's a chance that whatever happens
between the two in the forest earlier in the

00:03:35.799 --> 00:03:39.130
trailer, the fox survives the meeting to annoy
Gawain even further.

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:43.330
As befits the trailer's general air of mystery,
the nature of the giants remains very much

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:44.330
up in the air.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:47.900
Though their introductory shot shows them
just wandering, a later one shows one of them

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:48.980
reaching for Gawain.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:53.250
Did the knight intend to seek them out, or
did he just stumble in their dangerous path?

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.840
This remains to be seen.

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:59.819
A casual viewing of the trailer might give
you the impression that it gives away a whole

00:03:59.819 --> 00:04:01.379
lot of the plot of The Green Knight.

00:04:01.379 --> 00:04:05.380
However, the moments near the end make it
clear that the trailer only barely scratches

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:06.380
the surface.

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:09.980
The movie has plenty of big-name actors that
we barely see in the trailer.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:15.610
For instance, Joel Edgerton's Lord, Alicia
Vikander's Lady, and Erin Kellyman's Winfred.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:19.780
Toward the end of the trailer, we see a succession
of quick, adequately mysterious shots featuring

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:22.370
several of the hitherto unseen characters.

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:26.301
Lord, in particular, gets a quick shirtless
scene and later returns to ask Gawain what

00:04:26.301 --> 00:04:28.080
he hopes to gain from his mission.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.760
Gawain seems to have come a long way from
the opening moments of the trailer, since

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:34.880
his answer is clear and devoid of his earlier
hesitancy.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:37.120
He declares that he does his work for honor.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:38.120
Because:

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:40.910
"That is why a knight does what he does."

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:44.660
The trailer ends in pretty much the only way
it can.

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:48.940
As the last words of his heroic reply to the
Lord linger, we see Gawain enter some sort

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:51.970
of wooded area in which nature seems to have
taken over.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:56.370
The Green Knight awaits within, walking down
a set of stairs to meet Gawain and asks if

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.580
the knight is ready.

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:00.110
This, fortunately, isn't even close to a spoiler.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:04.090
Though the trailer offers a series of short,
exciting glimpses into the movie's world,

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:08.250
it does a commendable job at not revealing
anything beyond the most general outline of

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:09.250
the plot.

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:13.720
There are still many entirely unexplained
moments, such as the halo crown and the inexplicable

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:16.690
scene that features Gawain's head seemingly
catching fire.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:19.931
All in all, it seems that while The Green
Knight trailer gives glimpses of some of the

00:05:19.931 --> 00:05:24.590
film's secrets, it has also hinted at even
greater and deeper ones that you can't possibly

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.090
hope to comprehend without seeing the movie.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.800
That's the sign of a pretty great trailer.

